  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Accenture Federal Services obligated $167M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. Accenture Federal Services won 22 awards in the fiscal year so far, with an average award size of $7.6M. Accenture Federal Services obligations are down 95.2% year over year compared with prior full fiscal year totals. Accenture Federal Services shows a strong buyer concentration in FY2027 to date, with the Department of Veterans Affairs accounting for $151M of the current-year obligations. Accenture Federal Services also has smaller FY2027 to date obligations with the Department of Commerce at $7.7M and the Department of Homeland Security at $4.7M, alongside listed obligations of $1.9M and $1.7M with other agencies. Computer Systems Design Services is the top NAICS market for Accenture Federal Services, showing $167M in FY2027 to date. Historical context shows larger full-year obligations in prior periods: $2.7B in FY22, $2.9B in FY23, $3.4B in FY24, $3.2B in FY25, and $3.5B in FY26.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are Accenture Federal Services obligations by buyer?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $151M to Accenture Federal Services in FY2027 to date. The Department of Commerce obligated $7.7M and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $4.7M in the same period. Additional listed buyers show obligations of $1.9M and $1.7M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and historical context define Accenture Federal Services activity?",
        "body": "Computer Systems Design Services is the leading market for Accenture Federal Services with $167M in FY2027 to date. Prior fiscal years show higher full-year obligations for Accenture Federal Services, including $2.7B in FY22, $2.9B in FY23, $3.4B in FY24, $3.2B in FY25, and $3.5B in FY26."
      }
    ]
  },
